/*
 * $DOC$
 * $NAME$
 * GTI_DISPLAYSCALE
 *
 * $ONELINER$
 * Return the scale of the display
 *
 * $SYNTAX$
 * GtInfo( GTI_DISPLAYSCALE ) --> nScale
 *
 * $ARGUMENTS$
 * `GTI_DISPLAYSCALE` The selector, from gtinfo.ch.
 *
 * $RETURNS$
 * The scale set in the system for the monitor of the window, for example 1.5 for 150 %.
 *
 * $DESCRIPTION$
 * GTWVT returns the DPI of the monitor divided by 96.
 *
 * $NOTES$
 * Supported by GTWVT, GTSDL3, GTXWC and GTGLFW. On other terminals the result is NIL.
 *
 * $EXAMPLES$
 *
 * $OUTPUT$
 *
 * $CATEGORY$
 * Functions GT
 *
 * $HEADER$
 * gtinfo.ch
 *
 * $SEEALSO$
 * GTI_CONTENTSCALE, GTI_PIXELDENSITY
 *
 * $DOCEND$
 */
